- Q2 (the dry run, D2). Default: a dry run unless `--execute`. Alternative: send by default (one flag fewer for the first-run step 6; the first command of the tool that prints paper would then do so without being asked twice).
- Q3 (the pin and the port, D3). Default: both required; one port per run. Alternative: `--port 631 --port 443` in one run, one job per port (two pages printed per run; S6's "which port accepts" read in one go).
- Q4 (the document, D4). Default: synthetic only, 1 to 600 pages, default 1 (B1968 step 6's one-page print). Alternative: also `--file <pdf>` (a file read surface and a size bound to design; a later round).
- Q5 (the reason wrapper, D5). Default: `ReasonKeepingTransport` in the Print folder. Alternative: none (every transport failure reads `TransportFailed`, exit 7; the operator cannot tell a wrong pin from a closed port).
- Q6 (the records). Default: FOR RECORDS as written; the records seat files the registry comment (`CommandRegistry.cs:19`) and the named limits. Alternative: this lane fixes the comment (a second registry-file line, beyond the commission's one).
- Q7 (level, windows, pane and gate). Default: Opus by `<project>/CLAUDE.md:7`, `BRIEF_SEAT_LEVEL=opus`; READY at Step 0 + 110 minutes, the push by Step 0 + 80, a pane `Datasec/OXPd2-X53`, about 50 minutes of lock waits in all; the gate **G2** (the commission's rule; no new network or TLS code, MEASURED), on Opus (the project's every-agent rule), round 1 of 2 of lane L4; the seat's hard stop 23:30 AEDT by the commission. Alternative: G1, because the command is the lab tool's first write verb to a device (the gate then reads the dry-run branch and the six extra paths at G1 depth).
